step_details.raw_response:
Thought: Test a simple best_single ETS to see if a single strong model beats the mean baseline.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"best_single","model":"ETS"}

Thought: Test a median combination on the most stable pool (pool1) to see if it improves over the mean baseline.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"median","pool":"pool1"}

Thought: Test the strongest single model candidate, NaiveMovingAverage, to see if a simple best_single can beat the mean baseline.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"best_single","model":"NaiveMovingAverage"}

Thought: Test a trimmed mean over the full pool with 20% trimming to see if robust combination improves over mean baseline.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"trimmed_mean","pool":"pool_full","trim_pct":0.2}

Thought: Test a DTW barycenter on pool1 to see if a more sophisticated combination beats mean.

Action: evaluate_strategy

Action Input: {"combine":"dba","pool":"pool1","dba_max_iter":30}

Thought: Test a median combination over pool2 to see if it improves over mean baseline.

Action: evaluate_strategy

Action Input: {"combine":"median","pool":"pool2"}

Thought: Test a median combination on the most stable pool3 to see if it improves over the mean baseline.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"median","pool":"pool3"}

Thought: Test a weighted combination using inverse-error weights on a subset of the most stable models to see if it beats the plain mean.

Action: evaluate_strategy

Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","models":["ETS","THETA","ONLY_FT_catboost","ONLY_FT_rf","ARIMA"],"weights":"inverse_error"}

Thought: Test a simple mean over the pool4 models to see if a smaller subset mean beats the full mean baseline.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"mean","pool":"pool4"}

Thought: Test a simple median over pool4, as it may reduce variance and improve robustness in this trend‑dominated series.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"median","pool":"pool4"}

Thought: Test a trimmed mean on the compact pool4 to see if trimming improves over mean pool4.

Action: evaluate_strategy

Action Input: {"combine":"trimmed_mean","pool":"pool4","trim_pct":0.2}

Thought: Test a weighted combination using the pooled meta‑model handle w1, which may capture inter‑model relationships better than simple inverse‑error weighting.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","weights":"w1"}

Thought: Test a DTW barycenter on the more diverse pool2 to see if it beats the current trimmed mean.
Action: evaluate_strategy
Action Input: {"combine":"dba","pool":"pool2","dba_max_iter":30}

